103	   * curation tasks are the one standing use — each pacifies the warning with a
104	   * comment at its declaration site). It stays VALIDATED rather than ignored: a
105	   * deprecated field that silently accepts a typo mis-routes the dispatch to an
106	   * executor that declines it, and the task then never runs while the scheduler
107	   * re-arms it hourly.
108	   * @deprecated An executor's reach is how its repo is provisioned, never
109	   *   something a task asks for — drop the field; dispatches ride ready-for-agent.
110	   */
111	  if (decl.session_scope !== undefined && !SESSION_SCOPES.includes(decl.session_scope)) {
112	    bad(`"session_scope" ${JSON.stringify(decl.session_scope)} is not a legal session scope`, `drop it (dispatches ride ready-for-agent by default) — or, while it lingers, set one of: ${SESSION_SCOPES.join(', ')}`);
113	  }
114	
115	  // Prework (task-prework DESIGN §2) — OPTIONAL. The deterministic first phase
116	  // of task execution, a command the scheduler runs as a subprocess. When present
117	  // it must be a non-empty, task-local command AND carry a positive-integer
118	  // prework_timeout — the hard kill that bounds the subprocess.
